{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463063-convention-tradition-alliances","id":1463063,"title":"Convention-Tradition Alliances","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-07T23:42:21-07:00","id":1463063,"title":"Convention-Tradition Alliances","content":"The form this takes in my story is one of the Conventions who are opposed to the agenda of other Conventions quietly backing Tradition resistance to that agenda in a specific region. What Convention-Tradition Alliances have you used or considered using?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T13:29:11-07:00","id":1463141,"title":"","content":"On the Technocrat side, Void Engineers--and particularly those methodologies whose job is on the other side of the Gauntlet. On the Traditions side, my pick is basically any one of these: Etherites (and specifically, Ethernauts,) probably some kind of Virtual Adepts, and Ghost Wheel Society Dreamspeakers. You could probably make a lot of stuff work, but these are my picks for the most synergy/ease. My reasons are more or less as follow: There's already stuff in the books that says Void Engineers and Traditionalists tends to not be strictly KOS when they encounter each other far enough away from Earth, in addition to the fact that there's stuff in Revised that says the Void Engineers were sort of flirting with having one foot out of Union (though it might have been somewhat walked back in M20). And even beyond the actual metaplot stuff, the Void Engineer's ethos and raison d'\u00eatre feels somewhat less <i>evangelical </i>than the other conventions; the Void Engineers want to explore the Void and protect Earth. They probably also feel some affinity for the project of uplifting the masses and stamping out superstition, but what gets these people up in the morning is some combination of <i>Star Trek: Enterprise</i> and <i>Starship Troopers</i> (moreso the movie, than the the novel.) Anyway, I hope this is helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T16:05:55-07:00","id":1463171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463063-convention-tradition-alliances?p=1463141#post1463141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Technocrat side, Void Engineers--and particularly those methodologies whose job is on the other side of the Gauntlet. On the Traditions side, my pick is basically any one of these: Etherites (and specifically, Ethernauts,) probably some kind of Virtual Adepts, and Ghost Wheel Society Dreamspeakers. You could probably make a lot of stuff work, but these are my picks for the most synergy/ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my story, the Void Engineers are collectively dealing with a lot of guilt over wiping out so many spirits and umbral creatures in their quest to insulate sleepers from anything from the wrong side of the Gauntlet. If they were openly unrepentant about this, the Dreamspeakers would not easily accept them, except as necessary allies against the Nephandi. My plot with the Void Engineers has one seeking out the equivalent of Gaian Spirits native to other worlds, transporting them to Earth and working with a Progenitor to adapt them to the Earthly environment. The idea is that if Earth's atmosphere and ecology will inevitably change, why not establish new types of Gaian organisms that can stabilize the biosphere. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463063-convention-tradition-alliances?p=1463141#post1463141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reasons are more or less as follow: There's already stuff in the books that says Void Engineers and Traditionalists tends to not be strictly KOS when they encounter each other far enough away from Earth, in addition to the fact that there's stuff in Revised that says the Void Engineers were sort of flirting with having one foot out of Union (though it might have been somewhat walked back in M20).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Void Engineers leaving would break the Technocracy. The NWO and Syndicate focus on influencing the masses, often in direct competition. It-X, Progenitors and Void Engineers are, in my opinion, the physical-industrial heart of the Union (machines and buildings, biotech and clones, spaceships). The Progenitor NPC I mentioned has one foot out of the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463063-convention-tradition-alliances?p=1463141#post1463141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And even beyond the actual metaplot stuff, the Void Engineer's ethos and raison d'\u00eatre feels somewhat less <i>evangelical </i>than the other conventions; the Void Engineers want to explore the Void and protect Earth. They probably also feel some affinity for the project of uplifting the masses and stamping out superstition, but what gets these people up in the morning is some combination of <i>Star Trek: Enterprise</i> and <i>Starship Troopers</i> (moreso the movie, than the the novel.)</div> </div> </div> </div>An alliance with Etherites, Adepts and Dreamspeakers would move them closer to Enterprise. The Aquatic Xindi were a nice break from endless variations humanoid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463063-convention-tradition-alliances?p=1463141#post1463141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Anyway, I hope this is helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T19:05:10-07:00","id":1463183,"title":"","content":"One thing to keep in mind is that not everyone in the Union agrees with the idea that the ends justify the means to the same extent. They vary on where they put the line, but many will have it somewhere.<br /> <br /> For the Void Engineers allying with anyone in space is standard procedure against dangerous aliens, but you can have agents with a disposition to ally themselves with not-so-terrible RDs against evil-but-untouchable colleagues in any Convention. It-X is my favorite one, Progenitors are also easy to work this out. NWO will have the problem of dealing with their bosses and Syndicate depends a lot on how the local convention leans between Ideology and Greed, as they're consistently depicted as the most selfish Convention by far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T20:28:17-07:00","id":1463191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463063-convention-tradition-alliances?p=1463183#post1463183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to keep in mind is that not everyone in the Union agrees with the idea that the ends justify the means to the same extent. They vary on where they put the line, but many will have it somewhere.<br /> <br /> For the Void Engineers allying with anyone in space is standard procedure against dangerous aliens, but you can have agents with a disposition to ally themselves with not-so-terrible RDs against evil-but-untouchable colleagues in any Convention. It-X is my favorite one, Progenitors are also easy to work this out. NWO will have the problem of dealing with their bosses and Syndicate depends a lot on how the local convention leans between Ideology and Greed, as they're consistently depicted as the most selfish Convention by far.</div> </div> </div> </div>It-X is my favorite for this too and the one I'm using. They are opposed to the Syndicate's plans to extract a mountain range for all of its resources. I have a Syndicate character who is less interested in money, power and ideology than he is creating high quality television. He's a producer/writer/director. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T00:33:24-07:00","id":1463203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463063-convention-tradition-alliances?p=1463191#post1463191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It-X is my favorite for this too and the one I'm using. They are opposed to the Syndicate's plans to extract a mountain range for all of its resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty ugly move. You could have a biologist Progenitor in there worrying with the consequences to the ecosystem. But It-X is great.<br /> <br /> My favorite Mage character I ever played is a Dual Tradition Akashic Brotherhood/Iteration-X that left the Union disgruntled with the state of affairs there and went on a quest for self-discovery (and hiding. Lots of hiding). She's considerably messed up by trips to Room 101.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T20:07:36-07:00","id":1463278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463063-convention-tradition-alliances?p=1463203#post1463203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a pretty ugly move. You could have a biologist Progenitor in there worrying with the consequences to the ecosystem. But It-X is great.</div> </div> </div> </div>As dark as my imagination gets, I didn't draw it from there. It's a real thing: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VoOIB3_7bzU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VoOIB3_7bzU</a> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountaintop_removal_mining\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/MTR1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountaintop_removal_mining\" target=\"_blank\"> Mountaintop removal mining - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountaintop_removal_mining\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountaintop_removal_mining </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.salon.com/2021/05/01/we-still-blow-up-mountains-to-mine-coal-time-to-end-the-war-on-appalachia/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.salon.com/app/uploads/2021/04/west-virginia-mountain-removal-0430211.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.salon.com/2021/05/01/we-still-blow-up-mountains-to-mine-coal-time-to-end-the-war-on-appalachia/\" target=\"_blank\"> We still blow up mountains to mine coal: Time to end the war on Appalachia - Salon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.salon.com/2021/05/01/we-still-blow-up-mountains-to-mine-coal-time-to-end-the-war-on-appalachia/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.salon.com/2021/05/01/we-still-blow-up-mountains-to-mine-coal-time-to-end-the-war-on-appalachia/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The dying coal industry's last gasp is \"mountaintop removal\" mining &mdash; and it's even worse than it sounds </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I added the goal of using other non-fuel mined materials to build a Syndicate Funded Arcology Building, the first of many, that interests many Progenitors and It-X Macrotechnicians. My Genegineer NPC and Technocracy contact for the PCs has concluded that the ecosystem is falling apart and will need new organisms to be introduced to stabilize it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463063-convention-tradition-alliances?p=1463203#post1463203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite Mage character I ever played is a Dual Tradition Akashic Brotherhood/Iteration-X that left the Union disgruntled with the state of affairs there and went on a quest for self-discovery (and hiding. Lots of hiding). She's considerably messed up by trips to Room 101.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine the range of adventures that followed from her backstory. While the Technocracy tries to portray Traditions as culty, they are busy acting the part, Conditioning people into unquestioning obedience at the subject's expense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T08:16:25-07:00","id":1463318,"title":"","content":"If the threat is big enough the Trads and the Technos will ally. The issue is always, what happens when the Technos think the threat is over? That's when the Trads have to cut and run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}